			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Fix broken doc links and add missing doc comments\n\nFix cross-reference links in SendRequest and Multiplexer doc comments that referenced items not visible at their scope — `Shared::DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS` qualified as `crate::Client::Shared::DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS`, and private module references `PublishNotification::Fn` / `PublishNotificationFromMux::Fn` / `Multiplexer` stripped of link brackets since they are not `pub`.\n\nAdd an Architecture Reference section to Library.rs linking to the full protocol specification, and add doc comments to `Multiplexer::IsClosed()` and `Multiplexer::SideCarIdentifierBorrow()` describing their semantics.\n\nThe crate's rustdoc now renders without broken intra-doc links and surfaces the architecture guide entry point.",
			"SHA": "45ac334bf008b6600cfa7b872d688481d1a2d400"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T02:22:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2513,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Add GitHub badge bar and restructure funding/links section\n\nAdd a compact HTML badge table at the top of the README showing last-commit, issues, stars, and download counts for at-a-glance project status. Replace the old 2×2 SVG sponsor logo grid with a cleaner single-row table using updated asset paths and external NLnet banner URLs.\n\nConvert Related Documentation links from relative paths to absolute GitHub URLs pointing at the Current branch tree. Reflow long lines across multiple sections for consistent ~80-char wrapping.\n\nThe result is a more scannable, visually consistent README that surfaces GitHub metrics prominently and normalises the funding attribution layout.",
			"SHA": "6813d04cd58ac03a805b494470b68ce5c42d2662"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T00:05:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2513,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Rewrite README with consolidated tables and modern structure\n\nRemove the decorative HTML header/logo table and restructure the Vine README from a verbose, scattered layout into focused sections with tables. Key changes include: a compact Overview that folds in Key Features and Deep Dive prose, new Key Components and Service Definitions tables with file paths and gRPC method signatures, a Port Allocation table mapping processes to ports/protocols, an API Reference section, and a Related Documentation section with internal cross-links. The funding sponsor logo grid is replaced with a clean inline row, stale sections (Building & Running, standalone Changelog) are removed, and the footer is streamlined to a single line.\n\nThe result is a leaner, more scannable README that accurately reflects Vine's current state as a placeholder for protocol definitions and documents the real component locations.",
			"SHA": "99645e13032968c1fd4135cb36e6877b065eb1b0"
		}
	],
